- op: discuss  # 202e
  at: '2026-05-17T08:36:25Z'  # 202e
  by: agent  # 202e
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 202e
  clock: 3  # 202e
  nonce: 202e  # 202e
  message: "Closed as wont_do 2026-05-17 — premise gone stale. This item was filed in April after WI-ronot's ripgrep test produced a byte-identical SCIP symbol set when toggling procMacro flags. At the time we assumed rust-analyzer was engaging on both runs. The May 10 perf experiment (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_05102026_0400.md §3) discovered that rust-analyzer can silently fall through to tree-sitter when it crashes (e.g., wasmtime SIGKILL from memory pressure), in which case TWO failed runs would produce identical output telling us nothing about the procMacro flags. We cannot retrospectively validate the original WI-ronot result without re-running with an engagement check (no archived artifact). Separately, the May 10 experiment also empirically established that rust-analyzer DOES engage and emit origin=scip edges on candle (200K LOC, +174% edges vs tree-sitter) — so we already have proof that the backend produces non-tree-sitter information on real Rust code, which is what the downstream WI-burud / linker-upgrade work actually needed. The procMacro flag toggle is no longer on the critical path. Will refile if a downstream item surfaces a specific need to know proc-macro behaviour."  # 202e
